---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import MarketingChrome from "../../components/MarketingChrome.astro";

const phoneDisplay = "(501) 413-3386";
const tel = "tel:+15014133386";
const sms = "sms:+15014133386";
---

<Base
  title="Las Vegas Food Truck Websites, Free Demo | NV Labs"
  description="A free demo website for your Las Vegas food truck with your weekly schedule, menu, and catering requests. Call or text (501) 413-3386."
  image="/og.png"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <MarketingChrome>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Las Vegas food trucks</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">A website for your Las Vegas food truck that tells people where you'll be</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Free demo first. Weekly schedule, menu, and catering requests. Call or text to get started.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text me</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="where-title">
      <h2 id="where-title">"Where are you parked today?"</h2>
      <p>
        That's the question your fans ask most. Your website will answer it with a simple weekly
        schedule: where you'll be, what days, and what hours. Breweries, office parks, events,
        neighborhood spots. You text me changes or update it yourself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="menu-title">
      <h2 id="menu-title">A menu people can read before they're in line</h2>
      <p>
        Lines move faster when people already know what they want. I'll put your full menu on the
        site with short descriptions and photos of your best sellers. If you rotate specials, they
        get their own spot.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cater-title">
      <h2 id="cater-title">Catering and private events</h2>
      <p>
        Food truck catering is a big deal in Vegas. Weddings, office lunches, quinceañeras, block
        parties, school fundraisers. I'll add a catering page with a request form that asks for the
        date, location, number of guests, and type of event. That way you get the details you need
        to say yes or no quickly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="found-title">
      <h2 id="found-title">Getting found around the Valley</h2>
      <p>
        When someone in Henderson or Summerlin searches "food truck near me" or "food truck catering
        Las Vegas," you want to show up. I'll make sure your site clearly says you serve the Las
        Vegas area, the parts of town you hit most, and that it matches your Google Business
        Profile. No promises on rankings, but you'll be set up right.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="social-title">
      <h2 id="social-title">Works with your social media</h2>
      <p>
        You probably post your location on Instagram or Facebook already. Keep doing that. Your
        website gives you one link to share that always has your menu, schedule, and catering info,
        even for people who don't follow you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="local-title">
      <h2 id="local-title">I'm local, and it all happens by text</h2>
      <p>
        I'm based in Las Vegas, so I know the spots trucks hit around town. I build your demo and
        text you the link. Check it out between rushes. If you like it, I put it live. If not,
        nothing owed. We work by call and text.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div>
          <h3>My schedule changes every week. Can the site keep up?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes. I'll set up a schedule section that's quick to update, or you can text me the new
            week and I'll post it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Can people book my truck for events through the site?</h3>
          <p>
            They can send a catering request with all the details. You review it and reply when
            you're ready.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>I'm on Instagram already. Why do I need a site?</h3>
          <p>
            Instagram is great for daily updates. Your site helps people find you on Google,
            especially event planners searching for catering, and gives everyone one place for your
            menu and schedule.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
      <h2 id="cta-title">Let's get your truck online</h2>
      <p>Text me your truck's name and what you serve.</p>
      <a class="phone-big" href={tel}>{phoneDisplay}</a>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text</a>
      </div>
      <a class="back-home" href="/">Back to NV Labs home</a>
    </section>
  </MarketingChrome>
</Base>
